title: 'a-clock: iOS alarm platform wall, and pivot to nightstand mode (session close)'
summary: 'Closing a long session. Where things stand: the DESKTOP app is the fully-working product — installed at /Applications with a launchd KeepAlive agent, menu-bar tray, and rich alarms (beep, looping YouTube in a dedicated window, local audio/video files in the overlay), plus puzzle-to-dismiss, stopwatch/timer/pomodoro. Extended to iOS + Android via Tauri (one React codebase); the iOS app is signed (team SW4BMQ8PNL) and installed on a physical iPhone 15 Pro. The blocker we could not clear: a real lock-screen iOS alarm. iOS freezes the web app when the phone is locked, so only an OS notification can wake the user — but tauri-plugin-notification never DELIVERS scheduled local notifications on this setup. We confirmed mobile=true and perm=true, sendNotification returns success, yet nothing fires. We also found and worked around a genuine plugin bug (Schedule.at parses the UTC timestamp with a no-timezone DateFormatter, scheduling hours off) by switching to Schedule.interval with local calendar components — but delivery still failed, pointing to a deeper plugin/registration issue. Given that, we pivoted to ''nightstand mode'': a keep-screen-awake Wake Lock plus importing picked files into the app''s data dir (import_media) so they play in-app while a-clock is open on a charger. That build compiles and installs but was not device-verified before stopping. Also bumped the WebAudio beep volume. Not attempted: the native-Swift notification path and Critical Alerts entitlement.'
