decisions:
  - id: ios-nightstand-pivot
    decision: Accept that iOS lock-screen alarms aren't achievable via this Tauri/web stack; build nightstand mode (app-open) instead
    rationale: iOS freezes the web app when locked and the notification plugin won't deliver; the only reliable in-app path is keeping the screen awake so the JS scheduler runs and plays imported files while the app is open.
  - id: import-media
    decision: Copy picked files into the app data dir via an import_media command
    rationale: A raw picked path isn't playable in the iOS webview (sandbox/security scope); an app-owned copy is playable via the asset protocol and is durable on all platforms.
learnings:
  - 'iOS third-party lock-screen alarms are a hard wall: the OS freezes a backgrounded web app, so only notifications can wake you, and tauri-plugin-notification did not deliver scheduled local notifications here despite success returns.'
  - tauri-plugin-notification's Schedule.at parses the JS UTC timestamp with a DateFormatter that has no timezone (literal 'Z'), so it schedules in local time — hours off; Schedule.interval with local calendar components avoids that path.
  - 'For a web-wrapped iOS alarm the realistic model is nightstand mode: Wake Lock to keep the screen on + files imported into the app container for in-app playback.'
